<li><strong>March 4, 2026:</strong> In Balch Springs, the emergency manager reported several houses with water inside, with water rescues in Cedar Hill and Duncanville.</li>
<li><strong>June 19, 2026:</strong> Cars were submerged to the windshield at the Harry Hines and Spur 482 underpass, and intersections along Northwest Highway near Bachman Lake were flooded and closed.</li>
</ul>

<p>You can search these and other events with our <a href="/storm-history/">Dallas County storm history</a> tool.</p>

<h2>Flood vs. covered water damage: why the source matters</h2>

<p>For insurance purposes, not all water is the same. Most homeowners policies cover some kinds of sudden water damage and exclude others. The cause of the water, not how much damage it did, usually decides which policy responds.</p>

<table>
<thead><tr><th>Source of water</th><th>Homeowners policy (typical)</th><th>Flood policy (typical)</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Rising water from a creek, river, or lake</td><td>Excluded</td><td>Covered, subject to terms</td></tr>
<tr><td>Surface runoff from heavy rain entering the home</td><td>Excluded</td><td>Usually covered when it meets the policy’s flood definition</td></tr>
<tr><td>Rain entering through a wind- or hail-damaged roof or window</td><td>Often covered</td><td>Generally not</td></tr>
<tr><td>Sudden burst pipe or appliance supply line</td><td>Often covered</td><td>Not covered</td></tr>
<tr><td>Sewer or drain backup</td><td>Often excluded without an endorsement</td><td>Only when caused directly by flood</td></tr>
<tr><td>Long-term leak or seepage</td><td>Usually excluded</td><td>Not covered</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

<p>A single storm can involve more than one category. Hail can break a skylight while street water enters the garage. In those cases, two policies may each cover part of the loss, and clear documentation of where each kind of water came from becomes important. Our page on <a href="/services/water-damage-claims/">water damage claims</a> covers the non-flood side in more detail, and our guide to <a href="/freeze-damage-burst-pipe-claims-dallas/">freeze damage and burst pipe claims in Dallas</a> addresses plumbing failures.</p>

